<!--
  This file contains additional Special Units that will be added into the bottom of Ultimate Backup Menu (orange color)

  Improtant notes:

    # You may have as many as "SpecialUnit" tags as you want.

    # The "SpecialUnit" children nodes can consist of the mix from default regions (e.g. LocalPatrol, etc.) and custom regions (which requires "Zones"). Please refer to the existing examples

    # The "SpecialUnit" tag has the following attributes:
      - "name" is the name of the special unit which reflects the text in the menu entry (mandatory)
      - "role" is the role (AI) of that this special unit will play. Valid values are: "cop", "medic", or "fireman". (default="cop")
      - "code2" is the flag (True or False) whether this special unit will be added into "Code 2" response
      - "code3" is the flag (True or False) whether this special unit will be added into "Code 3" response
      - "pursuit" is the flag (True or False) whether this special unit will be added into "Pursuit" response
      - "traffic_stop" is the flag (True or False) whether this special unit will be added into "Traffic Stop" response
      - "felony_stop" is the flag (True or False) whether this special unit will be added into "Felony Stop" response

    # All "VehicleSets" (Vehicle & Ped, including weapons) definitions are the same as the ones in "DefaultRegion.xml" and "CustomRegions.xml"

    # The XML format in this file is similar with "DefaultRegions.xml". Please refer to descriptions on that xml file.

-->

